 takes an optional gitWorkspaceRoot (resolved from the tracker root when omitted, null keeps the old walk) and stops its .gitattributes walk at that top level, comparing each walked directory by real path so a symlinked tracker path keeps its patterns. pm health, pm validate and the workspace position read pass the root they already resolve. MERGE_SAFETY.md documents the bound; the SDK surface snapshot acknowledges the new parameter."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/close_reason","value":"Merge-fence evidence is bounded to the active Git worktree; an enclosing repository's fence never satisfies strict health"}],"before_hash":"d33bf0916f9cc8d08d0b7c3042931d0a2ce7fa45e536b24b38f2d26f5cbe2a25","after_hash":"3bd08d611495df04941a1168ebe8771a7184e539e5e35a0576833e13b503ac29","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"completion":{"timestamp":"2026-11-20T05:12:56.767Z","source":"close_time"},"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"66f52d61c4b7778b661c9520a5ff9b368b62c6221e2b87c11daa7aa5e937a882"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-20T05:12:57.341Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"f719b3080f29d4118076bddd","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1756","claim:pm-gh1757","claim:pm-gh1759","lineage:pm-gh1757","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1756+pm-gh1757+pm-gh1759","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1756","claim:pm-gh1757","claim:pm-gh1759","lineage:pm-gh1757","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.329","source":"probe"}},"op":"release","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-20T05:12:57.341Z"}],"before_hash":"3bd08d611495df04941a1168ebe8771a7184e539e5e35a0576833e13b503ac29","after_hash":"bf8ee545a460dafaec8e47a267bf542373629f679f56ae05d95c9d2b7dca57b5","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"maintenance","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"8c8aff21d7570f4a79df9f89062f3fc27eb5745eeeff846f91acf5442a183c82"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-20T05:34:32.129Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"f719b3080f29d4118076bddd","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.329","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-20T05:34:32.129Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review (gpt-6.2-sol, xhigh) of the first head raised five fence findings, all reproduced and fixed. (1) The logical walk could climb a symlink inside the worktree that points back at its root into the link's own parents (repo/sub/loop -> repo), where a stale sub/.gitattributes matched; the walk now follows the tracker's canonical path to the worktree's canonical top level, and patterns are computed from that ancestry. (2) Git stopped following in-tree .gitattributes symlinks in 2.32; the audit now reads only regular files there (lstat) and continues past a symlinked one. (3) A caller-supplied gitWorkspaceRoot is canonicalized, so a symlinked or 8.3-spelled root no longer yields a false not_installed. (4) findGitWorkspaceRoot stripped trailing spaces from Git's output with trim(); a worktree named with a trailing space then resolved to null and the default audit fell back to the unbounded walk; only the line terminator is stripped now. (5) Containment is judged by native path components rather than the backslash-normalizing isPathOutsideRoot. Inside Git the eight-level cap no longer applies (the walk ends at the top level), so a tracker nine levels down finds the root fence; outside Git the cap stays. Each case has a spec in fence-worktree-boundary.spec.ts."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-20T05:34:32.129Z"}],"before_hash":"bf8ee545a460dafaec8e47a267bf542373629f679f56ae05d95c9d2b7dca57b5","after_hash":"666ebec7681695c44e314ae4309d1bacadf5fb39950ab30e6d48530402a58a6a","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"4d5184c2e3ff1c9cb06d9b64d7e6acf97f52d2f16b1c51c19757a3d4378fbf24"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-20T05:34:46.124Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"f719b3080f29d4118076bddd","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.329","source":"probe"}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/contract_change/migrate","value":"No change for a fence at the worktree root or inside the same repository. To keep the old eight-level walk, pass { gitWorkspaceRoot: null }; a strict health check that newly fails needs pm merge install in that worktree, or a regular file in place of a symlinked .gitattributes"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/contract_change/after","value":"Inside a Git worktree the audit walks the tracker's canonical path up to the worktree's canonical top level (resolved from the tracker root, or passed as options.gitWorkspaceRoot) and reads only regular attribute files, so pm health, pm validate and the workspace position read report a linked worktree without its own fence as merge_fence_missing"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/contract_change/before","value":"The fence audit walked up to eight logical parents of the tracker root and accepted the first .gitattributes with a managed block, even one above the Git worktree top level or reached through a symlink, which Git never applies"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-20T05:34:46.124Z"}],"before_hash":"666ebec7681695c44e314ae4309d1bacadf5fb39950ab30e6d48530402a58a6a","after_hash":"c54371f73464e6def1b68f290b2cdbdff659c67131736ab02cfc57d218392196","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"b53509157e3849e17f9e58e7b270bc9f7d50cdbe855c98d106582e9ecf885830"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-20T05:51:56.257Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"f719b3080f29d4118076bddd","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.329","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-20T05:51:56.256Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 2 (gpt-6.2-sol, xhigh): three more findings fixed. (1) pm merge install followed a symlinked .gitattributes and reported unchanged when its target already held the block, while the audit (correctly) reports not_installed there, so the prescribed repair could not repair; reconcileGitattributesBlock now treats a symlinked file as changed, and the atomic rename replaces the link with a regular file holding the target's lines, leaving the target untouched (dry run reports changed). (2)+(3) Git path output is now parsed by one helper, stripGitPathTerminator, which removes exactly one LF (CRLF on Windows, where a name cannot hold a CR) for the show-toplevel, absolute-git-dir and driver-scope queries; resolveMergeDriverConfigScope asks for --git-dir and --git-common-dir in separate queries, so a clone whose name ends in a line break stays an ordinary clone with --local drivers instead of being misread as a linked worktree. Specs cover each; with the old combined parsing the line-break clone gains extensions.worktreeConfig (negative control)."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-20T05:51:56.257Z"}],"before_hash":"c54371f73464e6def1b68f290b2cdbdff659c67131736ab02cfc57d218392196","after_hash":"5b0d51e4463966c4b7242e24a9200f62ddb28eb51df8e4cdfa6c866e4e57a0a6","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"f793c9ea526558a9e0e5e0dbe10cf313b22a120e098d41344dc41842ab8a42e0"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-20T05:51:57.348Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"f719b3080f29d4118076bddd","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.329","source":"probe"}},"op":"files_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/files/6/note","value":"stripGitPathTerminator; separate git-dir and common-dir queries"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/files/6/path","value":"src/sdk/merge/worktree-config.ts"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/files/7","value":{"path":"tests/unit/sdk/merge/fence-worktree-boundary.spec.ts","scope":"project","note":"real-Git GH-1759 layout, in-repository nested fence, symlinked path and negative control"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-20T05:51:57.348Z"}],"before_hash":"5b0d51e4463966c4b7242e24a9200f62ddb28eb51df8e4cdfa6c866e4e57a0a6","after_hash":"67847d8e9842a36a32835ff8abb559c192621f2779f12cc678a9a874d2ffb2ee","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"maintenance","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"e97cad7bb9fe7481628ea05e9b03f69c7d176e03189566460e80ad6713a08447"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-20T06:02:37.384Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"f719b3080f29d4118076bddd","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.329","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/4","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-20T06:02:37.383Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 3 found no new defect in the fixes; one scope note recorded as a decision, not changed. Git's check-in attribute lookup falls back to the index when the working-tree .gitattributes is absent or (since 2.32) a symlink it refuses to open, so with a committed regular fence replaced by an unstaged symlink, git check-attr still reports pm-item-toon while the filesystem-only audit reports merge_fence_missing. That outcome is fail-closed, pm merge install resolves it by writing a regular file, and the audit never modelled the index fallback (a deleted but still indexed .gitattributes behaves the same way, before and after this change). The GH-1759 defect was a false success; modelling the index would add Git object reads to every health and validate run for a transient unstaged state."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-20T06:02:37.384Z"}],"before_hash":"67847d8e9842a36a32835ff8abb559c192621f2779f12cc678a9a874d2ffb2ee","after_hash":"33a3a5684df380c3112648cf38f48c9fd5a0985762f10e8299273c916d85253e","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"10aa61dd4ad9c989b152483a9b9e24c3191132402499643f874dfdc2928bb0a5"}
